   "text": "I read this as a vancomycin-type glycopeptide and wrote the SMILES region by region from the drawing.\n\n- **Left side chain:** an N-methylleucine is acylated onto the amino group of the first \u03b2-hydroxy-chlorotyrosine. That residue is linked through its C=O to the NH of an asparagine, which carries a CH2C(=O)NH2 side chain.\n- **Central ring:** a trisubstituted benzene bears the O-glucose in the middle, an aryl ether to the left chlorophenyl ring and one to the right chlorophenyl ring. Its benzylic CH is bonded to the Asn-derived NH and to a C(=O)NH leading into the right half.\n- **Right half:** two further aryl amino acids (a hydroxyphenylglycine and a dihydroxyphenylglycine) are joined by a biaryl bond and carry a free CO2H. The right chlorotyrosine's benzylic carbon carries an O-linked 4-keto-vancosamine-type sugar (3-amino-3-methyl-4-oxo, 6-methyl).\n- **Stereochemistry:** I encoded only the wedges actually drawn. These are the quaternary C(NH2)(CH3) of the amino sugar and, in the glucose, the C5 CH2OH and the C3 OH. The other stereocentres are drawn with plain bonds, so they carry no stereo marks.\n\nI derived the @/@@ signs from the drawn wedge geometry. The ring-closure digits are consistent, and the SMILES was not run through a parser.\n\nSMILES: CNC(CC(C)C)C(=O)NC1C(=O)NC(CC(N)=O)C(=O)NC(c2cc(O%10)c(OC3O[C@H](CO)C(O)[C@H](O)C3O)c(Oc3c(Cl)cc(cc3)C1O)c2)C(=O)NC4c5ccc(O)c(c5)-c6c(O)cc(O)cc6C(C(=O)O)NC(=O)C(NC4=O)C(OC8C[C@](C)(N)C(=O)C(C)O8)c7cc(Cl)c%10cc7"
